[profiles.guide]
notes = '''Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller. Press {lb} and {rb} together to switch the gyro off or on, and hold {r3} to recenter it.
Flick stick: push the right stick {rs} toward where you want to face and the view turns to it; turn it around the rim to keep turning. The gyro aims up, down and finely.
{start} (Escape) opens the game's menu and backs out of it. The game saves at checkpoints; it has no quick save.
{south} uses: doors, switches, pick-ups and turrets. Hold {south} to sprint. {east} jumps, {west} reloads and a long press of {west} changes the fire mode. {north} throws a grenade, and a long press of {north} picks the next grenade type.
{rb} is slow-mo (reflex time). {l3} toggles crouch, and it stays on until you click it again. {r3} is melee; tap {east} and then {r3} for a jump kick.
Hold {lb} for the weapon and grenade ring, aiming with the right stick {rs}. {left} and {right} step through your weapons. {up} switches the flashlight and {down} uses a med kit.
In the powered armor sections the same buttons drive the suit and fire its weapons. {select} (Tab) shows the players in multiplayer; chat needs typing: open the on-screen keyboard with {guide} + {west} and press T (all) or Y (team).
The mouse can feel smoothed and too fast; PCGamingWiki points to the FEAR 2 Mouse Fix for raw input. These are the game's default keys from a fan-made controls list and not checked in the game (fire mode, grenade type and sprint especially). The game also came out on the Xbox 360 and PlayStation 3; that layout isn't checked here, so the scheme follows the F.E.A.R. setup instead. Compare the keys with Options → Controls and change the buttons here to match. The Steam app id is from PCGamingWiki and the executable from Discord's game list. The gyro's full turn of 6000 is a guess, not worked out; if a turn of the controller doesn't turn the view as far, change it in the gyro settings.'''

